      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet, C1 (the input decoupling/bulk capacitor on the switched EPD rail, top plate on Display_Power_Switch, bottom plate on GND) is drawn with value 0.1 uF / 16 V.",
      "expected": "The specification's component-matching table lists C1 in the 1 uF / 25 V group ('C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default'), i.e. the PDI reference's default 1 µF/25 V input capacitor for the G1 boost stage. C1 should be 1 uF / 25 V.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: 'C1  0.1uF/16V' (capacitor from Display_Power_Switch to GND, beside C2 1uF/6.3V)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "C1 is 10x too small (and rated 16 V instead of 25 V) for the EPD boost-converter input rail. The reduced bulk capacitance on the switched Display_Power_Switch node can starve the boost converter (L1/Q1) of input charge during the high-current EPD refresh pulses, causing rail droop, unstable boost regulation and possible display artifacts; the lower voltage rating also erodes margin on a node that sees boost-converter transients.",
      "confidence": 0.66
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build otherwise matches the specification (EPD part values L1=10uH, R1=0.47R, Q1/U1/U2/U3, J1 signal mapping, FAN53610 topology, barrel-jack battery disconnect, S1-as-reset, Q2/R2 display power switch all check out), but C1 on the EPD_Driver sheet is drawn as 0.1 uF/16 V where the spec requires 1 uF/25 V, a 10x value and rating deviation on the boost-converter input rail."
}

